{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Scope refinement from operator: the runner-neutral bridge capability must be available through all three public surfaces (Python library, CLI, MCP) and from all supported install paths (pip wheel, Homebrew's wheel-backed formula environment, and MCP Registry/uvx install). Preserve scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py as a compatibility shim for checked-out workflows; provider wrappers should use an installed package entrypoint so clients do not need an unshipped repository script. Add RED-first interface-parity and wheel-content/install-path contract coverage before implementation."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786420192565397001,"uuid":"14e9d712-2897-428a-9576-208c630394da"}